            "review_title": "Review at Bia ZUBR",
            "review_text": "TheRealHanoian\nHanoi, Vietnam23 contributions\n0\na real Czech style place when you're craving for Eastern European food and drinks\nSep 2016 • Family\nWe unexpectedly walked in to a very true to itself Czech restaurant. \nHad a great dish of bread dumplings, the sauce was beyond words, the bread was so tender....and then here comes the owner.\nHe's been in Czech for 30 years (as so many Vietnamese are) and opened this restaurant for friends and family to gather more often.\nNow it's packed with many groups of customers, the expat community started to hear about this place and they just want to check it out right away. it was worth it.\n5 of us had 5 soups and 2 salad, 2 grilled pork dishes, 1 bread dumplings, 1 salami, 1 dish of cheese...for the price of $48...pretty good deal, eh.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten September 23, 2016",
